# Witness: an exclusion defined by an example inside a fenced code block

A bundle README that explains how to add an exclusion shows the whole table shape in a fence,
header and delimiter row and all. Scanning section 9 line by line with no fence tracking makes
that worked example DEFINE the identifier it illustrates - it is a well-formed exclusion table
in every respect except that it is an illustration - and a live citation of it is then
laundered by a template.

The unmeasured start-up path is recorded as EX-96.

## 9. Exclusions

| ID | Status | Exclusion |
|---|---|---|
| EX-01 | Open | The inbound half of the legacy-boundary rule is environment-conditional. |

An exclusion is added by appending a row to the table above, in this shape:

```
| ID | Status | Exclusion |
|---|---|---|
| EX-96 | Open | One sentence naming the limit, and what closes it. |
| EX-94 | Open | An identifier written inside a fence is an illustration, not a citation either. |
```
